From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam <i@noc.cat>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:10:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 67/70] remoteproc: qcom_sysmon: don't query a missing
 shutdown-ack interrupt

The shutdown-ack interrupt is optional, and the SC8280XP CDSP has none.
qcom_sysmon_shutdown_irq_state() asks the irqchip about it anyway. When
the PAS driver attaches to a running CDSP, that fails with:

  qcom_q6v5_pas 1b300000.remoteproc: failed to get shutdown_state: -22

Without the interrupt the subsystem cannot have signalled a shutdown, so
report false without asking.
---
 drivers/remoteproc/qcom_sysmon.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_sysmon.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_sysmon.c
index a0830a4..bab3474 100644
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_sysmon.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_sysmon.c
@@ -741,7 +741,8 @@ bool qcom_sysmon_shutdown_irq_state(struct qcom_sysmon *sysmon)
 	bool shutdown_state;
 	int ret;
 
-	if (!sysmon)
+	/* The shutdown-ack interrupt is optional; without it none was signalled */
+	if (!sysmon || sysmon->shutdown_irq <= 0)
 		return false;
 
 	ret = irq_get_irqchip_state(sysmon->shutdown_irq,
